2026-09-27T09:10:26.7701496Z Description:
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7702027Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7702534Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7703731Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7705202Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7705365Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7705686Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7706167Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7706604Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7706755Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7707108Z ================
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7707302Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7707574Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7708168Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7708524Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7708696Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7709134Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7709428Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7709639Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7710933Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7711511Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7712377Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7712951Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7713054Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7713491Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7714015Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7714286Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7714594Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7714988Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7788187Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7788622Z ========
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7788755Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7790412Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7791992Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7792244Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7792755Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7793661Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7794282Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7794891Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7795339Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7795773Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7795880Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7796132Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7796287Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7797361Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7798616Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7799270Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7800533Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:10:26.7800774Z 
